      "comment": "An each-way chance is taken with James Fanshawe's second string, Rift Valley, who gained my interest on her penultimate start when running on fourth of nine at Kempton. I thought the filly wasn't unduly pushed, and likewise in her last race at Wolverhampton where she finished last of all. The way she finished the Kempton race suggests this extra furlong will be ideal for her. First-time hood goes on, replacing tongue-tie. The trainer has been in good form lately with eight winners and ten places from the last forty runners."
